    {
      "id": "legend",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -270,
      "width": 2390,
      "height": 210,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "## Midterm 1 concept map\nEach box is a page of this site — click its title to open it, hover for a preview. Arrows read **“leads to”**; the label says how; plain lines link a box to the lecture that teaches it or to its sister problem. Top band: the time domain (Lectures 1–5). Middle band: the z-domain (Lectures 6–10). Bottom band: stability and causality (Lecture 11) and the exam problem families where all of it is tested.\n\nThree chains carry the exam: **δ → h → ∗ → LTI → H(z)** · **z-transform → ROC → sidedness → causality / stability** · **poles on the unit circle → marginal stability → unbounded outputs**."
    },
